Where the numbers come from

Every number in the rule files falls into one of the three groups below. A
rule with no number cannot be inspected, which is why the numbers are here
at all, and each one is attributed rather than asserted.

Accessibility guidelines — WCAG 2.2, level AA except where the entry says
otherwise.

  4.5 to 1, body text contrast                      rules/states.md
      SC 1.4.3 Contrast (Minimum)
  3 to 1, large text and non-text controls          rules/states.md
      SC 1.4.3 Contrast (Minimum); SC 1.4.11 Non-text Contrast
  24 by 24 CSS pixels, web tap target               rules/states.md
      SC 2.5.8 Target Size (Minimum)
  44 by 44 CSS pixels, web at the enhanced level    rules/states.md
      SC 2.5.5 Target Size (Enhanced), level AAA

Platform guidelines. Each platform states its own, and these are not the
accessibility figures above.

  44 by 44 points, Apple platforms                  rules/states.md
      Human Interface Guidelines, Accessibility: the default control size on
      iOS and iPadOS; the minimum stated there is 28 by 28
  48 by 48 density-independent pixels, Android      rules/states.md
      Android developers, Accessibility: "Use large, simple controls"

